0001   0000             ; Auxiliary-register range on the TMS320 family.
0002   0000             ;
0003   0000             ; Assembled twice: as "tms-arp-3225" with -3225, where it is clean, and as
0004   0000             ; "tms-arp-3210" with -3210, where the last two LAR lines are diagnosed.
0005   0000             ;
0006   0000             ; TWO SEPARATE MECHANISMS produce that difference, and they are easy to
0007   0000             ; conflate:
0008   0000             ;
0009   0000             ;   LARP uses the T1 rule with a validation mask taken from the table's OR
0010   0000             ;   column -- 0001 in tasm3210.tab, 0007 in tasm3225.tab. That difference comes
0011   0000             ;   from the TABLE, and the diagnostic is the generic
0012   0000             ;   "Range of argument exceeded."
0013   0000             ;
0014   0000             ;   LAR uses the TAR rule, whose ARP width is decided by a literal string
0015   0000             ;   comparison against the -<nn> OPTION TEXT: "3225" permits AR0-AR7, anything
0016   0000             ;   else permits only AR0-AR1. That is independent of the table's contents, and
0017   0000             ;   the diagnostic is the distinct "Range of ARP argument exceeded."
0018   0000             ;
0019   0000             ; This case pins both. It does not by itself separate them, since changing the
0020   0000             ; selector also changes the table. The isolating experiment -- one table file
0021   0000             ; copied under two selector names, giving different ARP widths from identical
0022   0000             ; bytes -- is recorded in the manual
0023   0000             ;
0024   0000             ; A reimplementation cannot derive the ARP width from the .tab file and must
0025   0000             ; special-case the selector. The TMS32010 has two auxiliary registers; the
0026   0000             ; TMS320C25 has eight.
0027   0000                     .org  0
0028   0000             
0029   0000             ; Table-driven mask (T1). Clean for both parts.
0030   0000 55 88               LARP  0
0031   0001 55 89               LARP  1
0032   0002             
0033   0002             ; Table-driven mask (T1). Out of range for the 32010's 1-bit field.
0034   0002 55 8A               LARP  2
0035   0003             
0036   0003             ; Selector-driven ARP width (TAR). AR0 and AR1 suit both parts.
0037   0003 30 0A               LAR   0,10
0038   0004 31 0B               LAR   1,11
0039   0005             
0040   0005             ; Selector-driven ARP width (TAR). AR5 and AR7 need the C25.
0041   0005 35 0C               LAR   5,12
0042   0006 37 0D               LAR   7,13
0043   0007             
0044   0007                     .end
tabasm: Number of errors = 0
